, "contribution_count": 287, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 3463425, "location_name": "Hanham", "location_name_detailed": "Hanham, United Kingdom"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2020-03-30", "published_at_date": "2020-03-30"}, {"review_id": 752004396, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r752004396-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Worth visiting but be careful of the guides that can rip you off!", "text": "I found the experience of this place quite profound.  However, the guide charged me double what he should have and that created a lot of fuss from the tourist office (they watched me and created the fuss - I didn't instigate it).  So, possibly best to get your information before you go and don't take a guide.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 3, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": null, "stay_date": "2020-03-31"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "3C680423955D647039834BE373A0E8E0", "name": "Catherine S", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/850CatherineS", "username": "850CatherineS", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/1a/f6/e7/99/default-avatar-2020-57.jpg", "contribution_count": 12, "hometown": null, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2020-03-29", "published_at_date": "2020-03-30"}, {"review_id": 751992859, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r751992859-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Best Hindus Temple", "text": "Pashupatinath temple is a one of the biggest Hindus temple in asia. Most visited places in Nepal. Recommend places.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": null, "stay_date": "2020-01-31"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "B6B7CC2712A371796B49E9C1BD51E4AC", "name": "Koon K", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/koonk2018", "username": "koonk2018", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/1a/f6/ef/73/default-avatar-2020-13.jpg", "contribution_count": 5, "hometown": null, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2020-03-29", "published_at_date": "2020-03-29"}, {"review_id": 751984101, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r751984101-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Quite interesting, but beware the tour guides", "text": "We visited this Hindu temple one morning around 9am. The complex itself is quite different than the Buddhist temples we visited in Kathmandu. It was obvious from the moment the taxi dropped us off that this would be a unique experience. \n\nYou will need to work your way past all of the street vendors selling both souvenirs and other items for offerings. Follow the path (and hoards of people) until you reach the ticket booth. As Western tourists, we were definitely in the minority here but we were there to learn about the temple, not to worship or mourn a loved one. Someone will stop you and have you purchase an admission ticket. The cost was 1,000 rupees, which we felt was worth the experience. \n\nIf you do not want a tour guide, you will need to stop the \"friendly\" local who begins talking to you and showing you the way to follow the path. If you choose to utilize the services of the guide, establish the price up front. This was pretty much how it seems to work at all of the major tourist sites in Kathmandu.\n\nI will say that we found the guide services to be worth the rupees spent. It was a bit expensive compared to some of the other site guides, but still a decent price. The guide we had was very thorough and explained quite a bit about the Hindu religion, the funeral process and the temple itself. If you decide to go on your own, you will probably wander around without truly understanding what you seeing.\n\nWe did have the opportunity to witness a funeral. The guide explained the process to us and we found it fascinating as it is completely different from what we are used to. There are also sadhus at the complex. Of course, in true Nepalese fashion, you can take pictures as long as you give them a donation. \n\nThis temple is definitely worth a visit, but make sure you go earlier in the day. They close from noon-5pm each day. If you want to see the funeral process, make sure to be there by 10am.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 4, "subratings": [], "like_count": 3, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": null, "stay_date": "2019-12-31"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "3A9A7FB610B4D9EEF4B012394339B69E", "name": "KentuckyGirlAtHeart", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/KentuckyGirlAtHeart", "username": "KentuckyGirlAtHeart", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/1d/c4/2f/f6/kentuckygirlatheart.jpg", "contribution_count": 143, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 294013, "location_name": "Abu Dhabi", "location_name_detailed": "Abu Dhabi, United Arab Emirates"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2020-03-29", "published_at_date": "2020-03-29"}, {"review_id": 751905946, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r751905946-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Spiritual journey ", "text": "Another wonderful temple simply loved its architecture and woodwork very nice it’s a surely must visit place ", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 1, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "couples", "stay_date": "2020-02-29"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "2D4DEF8D05E7DAD5A589B19B515761C9", "name": "Sightsee737349", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/Sightsee737349", "username": "Sightsee737349", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/1a/f6/7c/01/default-avatar-2020-5.jpg", "contribution_count": 564, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 1092107, "location_name": "McLeod Ganj", "location_name_detailed": "McLeod Ganj, India"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2020-03-27", "published_at_date": "2020-03-27"}, {"review_id": 751669658, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r751669658-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Cultural Insight", "text": "This location felt very sacred and crucial to the local people. It is not to be visited without careful consideration, as it is the location at which many people cremate their loved ones. It was a very moving experience for me to witness families saying goodbye, leaving tributes and placing their family member on an old style timber pyre, then cremating them before my very eyes.\n\nThis experience is not for everyone. But for me, it was very worthwhile.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": null, "stay_date": "2020-03-31"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "4CBB8138DD20E244709BC5A66B049031", "name": "Cablon", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/Cablon", "username": "Cablon", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/1b/32/d7/20/cablon.jpg", "contribution_count": 16, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 255100, "location_name": "Melbourne", "location_name_detailed": "Melbourne, Australia"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": []